How spring boot calls External Api>>

There are major 4 types>>

1> RestTemplate

. > introduced in spring 3.0 framework
. > Used in heavily Spring boot 2.x
. > Deprecated in Spring 5+
. > work synchronize like first it took response then do other work
. > Still found in 90 percent enterprices codebase
. > Thread waits until Api response (Blocking state)

2> WebClient

.>Introduced in spring FrameWork 5.0
.>Recommended approach
.>Non Blocking
.>Reactive (uses Project Reactor)
.>Work in mono and flex

3> Rest cLint

,>Introduced in spring Framework 6.1
.>Preferred blocking client
.>Designed for spring boot 4
.>Modern and fluent api
.>Replaces RestTemplate officialy

4> HttpExchange

.> Declarative Approch
.> spring 6
.> Similar to Feign but Spring Native(we create an interface declare there implementation and only call them)
   this is of spring own implementation(Native)
.> Clean and Readable code
.> Internally uses webclient

